  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "We have native eye tracking support now and that's great!\n\nThough I feel like it should be used to it's full potential more via menu interactions.\n\nThe idea:\n\nUse eye gaze data to act like another pointer for menus and world interaction.\n\nThere could be a setting to allow for a trigger on your (left or right) controller to trigger ET gaze pointer click.\n\nIdeally there would also be an OSC address to toggle this externally. (say the external eye tracking software like EyeTrackVR can send a click when the user winks)\n\nFor example with the setting on, looking at the \"worlds\" button and an app sending a True value to the OSC address: \"/tracking/eye/PointerClick\" would cause a trigger press on that button.\n\nThanks for your time.",
